<title>AUSTRALIA: Woodside half year net profit jumps.</title>
<headline>Woodside half year net profit jumps.</headline>
<dateline>PERTH 1996-09-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		   145.06 vs 103.14</p>
<p>    Net				     84.38 vs 43.32</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)		     6.00 vs 4.00</p>
<p>NOTE: Woodside Petroleum Ltd is the operator of the North West Shelf gas project offshore Western Australia and is about 40 percent owned by the Royal Dutch Shell group  </p>
<p>    Sales				  366.74 vs 288.62</p>
<p>    Other income			  24.01 vs 26.76</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			   12.7  vs 6.5</p>
<p>    Abnormal items		  loss 7.68 vs nil</p>
<p>Dividend is unfranked</p>
<p>Pay date November7</p>
<p>Reg date October 23</p>
<p>    Tax				     58.53 vs 59.88</p>
<p>    Interest				42.22 vs 57.87</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  90.71 vs 71.43</p>
<p>    Minorities				nil vs nil</p>
</text>
